      "text": "A fierce public dispute erupted after a casting announcement placed a performer in the roles of Helen and Clytemnestra. In the cold, public sphere where intimate stories are torn apart, cultural critics attacking a love story's portrayal leveled public accusations against the film project, claiming it erased a shared heritage. Defenders countered with a cultural claim, arguing for love stories belonging to all humanity. The resulting societal debate has turned a classic epic into a flashpoint over identity and belonging.",
